The split runs last in build_segments, after _merge_short and _split_long, so merging short lines (needed so translation sees whole phrases) can never rebuild a segment the split just cut. It splits nearest the middle rather than at the biggest pause or greedily at the limit: both parts end up about the same length, so neither is a short fragment and recursion only goes as deep as needed. The middle is measured in characters when the text is too long and in time when only the duration is, because those are the two limits a viewer actually hits. It works on words (phrases from groupers/ for ja/zh), so it can never cut inside one; a single over-long word is kept rather than broken. The limits are constants, not config settings, until someone needs to change them; the pipeline fingerprints settings, not code, so existing work folders keep their old segments until --force.
